Q: Problem with dynamic submenus: can&#39;t achieve a static reference from one sheet to another A: <p>I still don't know if this can be done, and this is really just a work around, but in case someone comes across this I wrote a simple Apps Script and put it in a menu item to reset all the dropdowns as a stop gap so the user can still use the sheet if they drag rows around.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const reset = function() {
    let sheet1 = ss.getSheetByName(&quot;Sheet 1&quot;);
    for (let i = 1; i&lt;=sheet1.getLastRow(); i++) {
      let rangeToReset = sheet1.getRange(i, 2);
      let rangeToReference = ss.getRange(&quot;Sheet 2&quot;+i+&quot;:&quot;+i);
      let rule = SpreadsheetApp.newDataValidation().requireValueInRange(rangeToReference).build();
      rangeToReset.setDataValidation(rule);
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

Q: google_mlkit_face_detection: FaceDetector.processImage() crashes only in Android release (works in debug) A: <p>I ran into this exact issue on Android release builds. It's an R8 minification problem. ML Kit uses reflection to load some internal face detection classes, and R8 strips or renames them in release builds. Debug builds skip R8 shrinking, which is why it works fine there.</p>
<p>You need to add ProGuard/R8 keep rules for ML Kit.</p>
<p>Create or open <code>android/app/proguard-rules.pro</code> and add:</p>
<pre><code>-keep class com.google.mlkit.** { *; }
-keep class com.google.android.gms.internal.mlkit_vision_face.** { *; }
-keepclassmembers class * { @com.google.mlkit.** &lt;methods&gt;; }
-dontwarn com.google.mlkit.**
-dontwarn com.google.android.gms.**
</code></pre>
<p>Then make sure your <code>android/app/build.gradle</code> release build type is configured to use these rules:</p>
<pre><code>buildTypes {
    release {
        minifyEnabled true
        shrinkResources true
        proguardFiles getDefaultProguardFile('proguard-android-optimize.txt'), 'proguard-rules.pro'
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Run <code>flutter clean</code> before building the release APK again, otherwise Gradle might use the cached dex output and the crash will persist.</p>
